      "category": "src_content",
      "full_page": "NOTE: With a tinge of fraternal humor, the following letter -- at once poetic, yet decidedly earnest -- will be found a relief for any color of the \"blues\" (in season). A missionary in the Philippines, Rev. Edward Casey, writes an elder brother, Rev. Maurice Casey, at the time in Yonkers, N. Y. The latter, having resumed studying after twenty years vacation continued with the younger and was ordained just a year before him. Then after eighteen years of pastoral and missionary work joined the Capuchin Order as Fr. Joachim. The \"K\" - \"C\" used as an example, is at the same time familiar to the brothers as an equivalent of Casey.",
      "per_polygon": "NOTE: With a tinge of fraternal humor, the following letter -- at once poetic, yet decidedly earnest -- will be found a relief for any color of the \"blues\" (in season). A missionary in the Philippines, Rev. Edward Casey, writes an elder brother, Rev. Maurice Casey, at the time in Yonkers, N. Y. The latter, having resumed studying after twenty years vacation continued with the younger and was ordained just a year before him. Then after eighteen years of pastoral and missionary work joined the Capuchin Order as Fr. Joachim. The \"K\" - \"C\" used as an example, is at the same time familiar to the brothers as an equivalent of Casey.",
