    {
      "rid": "doc_1.archv_commentary.1",
      "doc": "doc_1",
      "category": "archv_commentary",
      "full_page": "( Father Solanus wrote this prologue to the rhyme-letter of Msgr. Edward Casey as a little explanation. Father Solanus had copies made by some of his friends, as he did at other times with certain interesting, inspirational letters which he found useful to give to people when it might benefit their state of mind. A copy of this rhyme-letter was for a long time in the Monastery Office in Detroit for people to read while waiting for Fr. Solanus. Appears on #1009 of Msgr. Edw. Casey's letters)",
